coder › Done. Committed as `938eb96` on `work/main`.

**What changed:**

- **`src/tokenize.ts` (new)** — exports `tokenize(text)` using exactly the plan's implementation: `text.toLowerCase().split(/[^a-z0-9']+/).filter((word) => word !== '')`, with a doc comment.
- **`src/stats.ts`** — both functions now import and use `tokenize`. `wordCount` returns `tokenize(text).length` (results unchanged, since it was the same tokenization). `topWords` counts `tokenize(text)` tokens in a Map and sorts with `(a, b) => b[1] - a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0])`, then `slice(0, n)`; old inline whitespace-split tokenization removed.
- **`src/stats.test.ts`** — kept the existing `wordCount` test; added: case-insensitive counting (`topWords('The the THE cat', 10)` → `[['the', 3], ['cat', 1]]`) and alphabetical tie-breaking (`topWords('zebra apple mango', 10)` → apple, mango, zebra).
- **`src/tokenize.test.ts`** (new) — lowercasing and apostrophes kept (`tokenize("Don't stop. DON'T!")` → `["don't", "stop", "don't"]`), and punctuation/spaces as separators with no empty entries (`tokenize('one, two;three   four')`).

